  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONTINUING THE DEVELOPMENT OF ELEPHANT AND OTHER WILDLIFE VETERINARY TEACHING, TRAINING, AND RESEARCH CAPACITIES, AND AN ELEPHANT AND WILDLIFE AMBULANCE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE GOAL OF THIS PROJECT IS TO ACHIEVE SUSTAINABLE PROVISION OF PROFESSIONAL VETERINARY SERVICE TO SUPPORT ELEPHANT AND OTHER WILDLIFE CONSERVATION PROGRAMS AND ACTIVITIES IN SUMATRA BY BUILDING LOCAL CAPACITY AND THROUGH DIRECT HANDS-ON SUPPORT. SPECIFIC OBJECTIVES ARE AS FOLLOWS: 1) CONTINUE WILDLIFE SPECIFIC VETERINARY EDUCATION AND TRAINING AT THE PREVIOUSLY ESTABLISHED CENTER FOR WILDLIFE STUDIES AND ITS PROGRAM FOR WILDLIFE AND CONSERVATION MEDICINE AT THE VETERINARY FACULTY OF THE SYIAH KUALA UNIVERSITY BANDA ACEH IN COLLABORATION WITH NATIONAL AND INTERNATIONAL EXPERIENCED WILDLIFE VETERINARIANS AND 2) TO CONTINUE THE WILDLIFE AMBULANCE PROGRAM WHICH HAS BEEN ESTABLISHED AT SYIAH KUALA UNIVERSITIES VETERINARY FACULTY AND PROVIDE VETERINARY EXPERTISE AND SERVICES NEEDED FOR ELEPHANT AND OTHER WILDLIFE CONSERVATION AND WELFARE PROGRAMS CONDUCTED BY GOVERNMENT AND NON-GOVERNMENT INSTITUTIONS IN SUMATRA.</narrative>
  </description>
